--- docs/protocol.md
     1	# Client protocol
     2	
     3	The server sends events over the socket as {type, payload}.
     4	
     5	| type | payload |
     6	|---|---|
     7	| message | id, userId, text, sentAt |
     8	| message.deleted | id |
     9	| typing | userId |
    10	| presence | userId, status |
    11	
    12	Android clients older than 5.2 (about 30 percent of installs) decode message payloads with a strict
    13	schema and crash on any field they don't know. Every client ignores event types it doesn't know.

